# Launch checklist

## Product and evidence

- [ ] Validate the manifest and review every approved public claim.
- [ ] Complete desktop and mobile browser smoke checks.
- [ ] Complete keyboard-only and screen-reader spot checks.
- [ ] Verify analytics payloads contain no answers, email, or free text.
- [ ] Confirm optional lead transport and safe failure behavior.
- [ ] Capture current screenshots and a 90-second demo.
- [ ] Recheck proof links: {{proof_links}}

## Channel preparation

- [ ] Read current Product Hunt, Show HN, Reddit, DEV, GitHub, Slack, and Discord rules before posting.
- [ ] Ask community moderators when promotional fit is unclear.
- [ ] Customize each draft for the audience; do not cross-post identical copy at once.
- [ ] Prepare founder responses for technical questions and limitations.
- [ ] Verify every direct contact and record the public relevance reason.

## Launch and follow-up

- [ ] Soft-launch to a small technical group first.
- [ ] Fix material confusion before broad distribution.
- [ ] Space channel launches across the calendar.
- [ ] Reply substantively; do not manufacture engagement.
- [ ] Send at most one relevant three-business-day follow-up.
- [ ] Review starts, completions, CTA clicks, qualified leads, and objections weekly.
- [ ] Record content insights back into the manifest, FAQ, and queue.
